dhru-vá, a. [√ dhṛ] firm, stable, constant;
 🞄permanent, perpetual, fixed, immutable;
 🞄certain, inevitable: -m, ad. certainly, assuredly;
 🞄m. polar star: personified as the son of 🞄Uttānapāda grandson of Manu.

dhruva-śīla, a. permanently resident;
 🞄not changing oneʼs residence;
 -saṃdhi, m. N.;
 -siddhi, m. (sure recovery), N. 🞄of a physician.
